From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: kernelbase, conhost: a pseudo console's programs get its handles, and it resizes

Windows Terminal and every other ConPTY host start their shells on a pseudo
console (CreatePseudoConsole, PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_PSEUDOCONSOLE) and leave
the standard handles alone. On Windows a console program started on a
console is on a new console: it does not share its parent's standard
handles and, given none, uses the console's. Wine connected the program to
the pseudo console but gave it its parent's handles (none, for a terminal),
so cmd and PowerShell wrote nowhere and read nothing. CreateProcess now
drops the parent's handles for a pseudo console child (unless
STARTF_USESTDHANDLES names some) and marks it (a Wine-private
ConsoleFlags bit, cleared at start-up so it is not inherited further), and
init_console opens the console's handles for such a console program, as it
does for a new console. A program that merely inherits its parent's console
with no handles still gets none (kernel32:console's with_console_tests[18],
Windows' own result).

ResizePseudoConsole was a FIXME returning E_NOTIMPL. It now sends conhost
the resize signal Windows' conhost reads on its signal pipe (8, then the
width and height), and conhost resizes the screen buffer and its window,
tells the program (WINDOW_BUFFER_SIZE_EVENT, when it asked for them) and
repaints the terminal from the buffer.

Gate: sg-shell's test/terminal-check.sh (cmd and PowerShell 7 in a
terminal's tabs; a program sees the new size after the window grows).
Stock wine-sg shows no prompt at all.
---
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/console.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/console.c
@@ -2327,8 +2327,18 @@
  */
 HRESULT WINAPI ResizePseudoConsole( HPCON handle, COORD size )
 {
-    FIXME( "%p (%u,%u)\n", handle, size.X, size.Y );
-    return E_NOTIMPL;
+    struct pseudo_console *pseudo_console = handle;
+    /* the signal pipe's message, as Windows' conhost reads it: the resize
+     * signal (8), then the new width and height */
+    unsigned short msg[3] = { 8, size.X, size.Y };
+    DWORD written;
+
+    TRACE( "%p (%u,%u)\n", handle, size.X, size.Y );
+
+    if (!pseudo_console || !pseudo_console->signal || !size.X || !size.Y) return E_INVALIDARG;
+    if (!WriteFile( pseudo_console->signal, msg, sizeof(msg), &written, NULL ) || written != sizeof(msg))
+        return HRESULT_FROM_WIN32( GetLastError() );
+    return S_OK;
 }
 
 static BOOL is_tty_handle( HANDLE handle )
@@ -2385,5 +2395,15 @@
             alloc_console( no_window );
     }
     else if (params->ConsoleHandle && params->ConsoleHandle != CONSOLE_HANDLE_SHELL_NO_WINDOW)
-        create_console_connection( params->ConsoleHandle );
+    {
+        /* A console program started on a pseudo console (terminals start
+         * their shells so) is on a new console, as on Windows: with no
+         * standard handles of its own it uses the console's. One that merely
+         * inherits its parent's console does not. */
+        BOOL pseudo = params->ConsoleFlags & CONSOLE_FLAGS_PSEUDO_CONSOLE;
+        params->ConsoleFlags &= ~CONSOLE_FLAGS_PSEUDO_CONSOLE;     /* not for our own children */
+        if (create_console_connection( params->ConsoleHandle ) && pseudo &&
+            RtlImageNtHeader( GetModuleHandleW( NULL ))->OptionalHeader.Subsystem == IMAGE_SUBSYSTEM_WINDOWS_CUI)
+            init_console_std_handles( FALSE );
+    }
 }
